# ====================================================================
# Calendar & Cloud Integration Configuration
# ====================================================================
# Copy this file to .env or .env.local to activate live OAuth 2.0 syncing
# for Google Calendar and Microsoft 365 Outlook.
#
# If left blank, the app runs in instant Sandbox Mode, simulating full
# calendar imports and syncing without requiring developer credentials.
# ====================================================================

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. GOOGLE CALENDAR (Google Cloud Console)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Go to: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Create or select a project.
# 3. Enable the "Google Calendar API":
#    APIs & Services > Library > Search "Google Calendar API" > Enable
# 4. Configure OAuth Consent Screen:
#    - User Type: External (or Internal if Google Workspace organization)
#    - Add Scopes: 
#      • https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.readonly
#      • https://www.googleapis.com/auth/userinfo.email
#      • https://www.googleapis.com/auth/userinfo.profile
# 5. Create Credentials > OAuth Client ID:
#    - Web Application: For Web / Expo development browser
#      Authorized redirect URI: https://auth.expo.io/@<your-expo-username>/hacker-wrath
#    - iOS (Optional for production standalone builds):
#      Bundle Identifier: com.anonymous.hackerwrath
#    - Android (Optional for production standalone builds):
#      Package Name: com.anonymous.hackerwrath
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_WEB=your_google_web_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_IOS=your_google_ios_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID_ANDROID=your_google_android_client_id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. MICROSOFT 365 OUTLOOK (Microsoft Entra ID / Azure Portal)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Go to: https://portal.azure.com/#view/Microsoft_AAD_IAM/ActiveDirectoryMenuBlade/~/RegisteredApps
# 2. Register an application:
#    - Name: HackerWrath Calendar Sync
#    - Supported account types:
#      "Accounts in any organizational directory (Any Microsoft Entra ID tenant - Multitenant) and personal Microsoft accounts (e.g. Skype, Xbox)"
#    - Redirect URI (Platform: Mobile and desktop applications):
#      • hackerwrath://auth
#      • https://auth.expo.io/@<your-expo-username>/hacker-wrath
# 3. API Permissions:
#    - Microsoft Graph > Delegated permissions:
#      • Calendars.Read (Read user calendars)
#      • User.Read (Sign in and read user profile)
#      • offline_access (Maintain access to data)
# 4. Copy the "Application (client) ID" into EXPO_PUBLIC_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID
# --------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=your_microsoft_application_client_id
EXPO_PUBLIC_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=common
